{
	"_comment": "The one table naming a keyboard key or modifier in visible text, on every driver and web page. `keys` maps each key id to the locale key of its human name; `platforms` names the locale key a driver shows instead, where that OS calls the key otherwise (Option for Alt on macOS, Super for the system key on Linux; the chord notation's `cmd` is the system key, so it reads Win on Windows and Super on Linux). `macos_symbol` is the glyph the macOS menus draw for a modifier where they already use symbols (⌃⇧⌥⌘), one spelling for every such place. `aliases` maps every other spelling a driver, a config file or a slot id uses to its key id. tools/codegen/codegen-key-names.cjs projects it for Lua and AutoHotkey; tools/test/test-key-names-single-source.cjs holds the projections, the catalogue and the 21 locales to it. Keycap legends drawn on a keyboard picture (layer_editor.key.*) are short on purpose and are not row text.",
	"keys": {
		"escape": { "i18n": "key_name.escape" },
		"tab": { "i18n": "key_name.tab" },
		"caps_lock": { "i18n": "key_name.caps_lock" },
		"enter": { "i18n": "key_name.enter" },
		"space": { "i18n": "key_name.space" },
		"backspace": { "i18n": "key_name.backspace" },
		"delete": { "i18n": "key_name.delete" },
		"fn": { "i18n": "key_name.fn" },
		"shift": { "i18n": "key_name.shift", "macos_symbol": "⇧" },
		"left_shift": { "i18n": "key_name.left_shift" },
		"right_shift": { "i18n": "key_name.right_shift" },
		"ctrl": { "i18n": "key_name.ctrl", "macos_symbol": "⌃" },
		"left_ctrl": { "i18n": "key_name.left_ctrl" },
		"right_ctrl": { "i18n": "key_name.right_ctrl" },
		"alt": {
			"i18n": "key_name.alt",
